# _headers — Netlify's header config file. Ignored by other hosts (GitHub
# Pages, S3) — those need equivalent config at the host/CDN level if you use
# them instead. See firebase.json for the Firebase Hosting equivalent, and
# vercel.json for Vercel.
#
# I have not tested this against a live Netlify deploy — after publishing,
# check response headers with your browser's network tab or
# https://securityheaders.com to confirm these are actually being applied.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
